lines+=['','FFA supplies the largest favorable8/12 mean, but its interval is widest. No format independently establishes an improvement. Across complete blocks,8/12 has positive means in7generator families and negative in5;8/8 splits6and6. Family cells are descriptive, not independently tuned policies.','', '|Paired comparison|Higher score|Identical score|Lower score|Absolute change≥1pp|Absolute change≥5pp|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for name,v in main['policy_contrasts'].items():
 ds=[100*x['delta']for x in v['paired_entries']];lines.append(f"|{name}|{sum(x>0 for x in ds)}|{sum(x==0 for x in ds)}|{sum(x<0 for x in ds)}|{sum(abs(x)>=1 for x in ds)}|{sum(abs(x)>=5 for x in ds)}|")
lines+=['','Every comparison has median score difference zero.8/12 leaves62.2%of scores exactly equal;8/8 leaves31.4%equal. This establishes a larger frequency of score changes under8/8, not proof that a cap never bound in tied games or that intermediate states/orders were identical.','', '![Primary effects and actual worker activity](strength-and-worker-allocation.png)','', '## All-case food and labor','', 'Each scenario is truncated at the latest exact counter publication common to all three arms before the shortest game ends. No extrapolation, interpolation or post-stop fill. Rates use10,000shared observed ticks; worker death rates use actual worker exposure. Population uses its separately recorded common state timestamp. These are observed-window mechanisms, not counterfactual full90k trajectories. All designed scenarios enter coverage; no hunger/changed-game/outcome selection. Many secondary intervals are unadjusted for multiplicity.','', '|Metric|Unit|Baseline|8/12|8/12 change95% interval|8/8|8/8 change95% interval|','|---|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---|']
metrics=['swarm_workers','inn_workers','swarm_share','inn_share','site_share','idle_share','worker_births','births','meals','harvested','delivered','starvation','worker_starvation_rate','population','combat','net_conversions']
for metric in metrics:
 a=next(r for r in rows if r['scope']=='subject'and r['format']=='equal_format'and r['candidate']=='inn8-swarm12'and r['reference']=='baseline'and r['metric']==metric);b=next(r for r in rows if r['scope']=='subject'and r['format']=='equal_format'and r['candidate']=='inn8-swarm8'and r['reference']=='baseline'and r['metric']==metric)
