lines+=['', 'Worker equivalents are colonywide actual supplying activity, not a per-building requested cap. Under8/12, swarm activity falls0.169workers (~1.7%) and inn activity rises0.080, with its interval including zero. Under8/8, swarm activity falls1.190workers (~12.1%), while inn activity changes−0.162with uncertainty spanning zero. The8/8 healthy-idle share increases0.673pp and construction-supply share0.439pp. These activity changes do not track individual workers from one job to another. They show that lower swarm demand is not automatically converted into additional meal service.','', 'Swarm8 reduces worker births by1.157/10kticks (~3.9%) and total births by1.047; the latter reduction has interval[−1.647,−0.467]. Spawning wheat falls mechanically with births and is not an independent confirming metric.8/12 preserves births almost unchanged. Raising the swarm ceiling8→12 while holding inn8 fixed gives1.031more total births/10k[+0.443,+1.593] and1.022more active swarm workers[+0.566,+1.556], without a demonstrated score improvement. The evidence is consistent with a throughput/growth throttle under8, rather than broad proof of allocator repair.','', 'Under8/12, meals rise0.670wheat/10k (~0.94%), exploratory interval[+0.136,+1.378]. FFA supplies most of this signal: +1.941[+0.321,+4.122], versus−0.086in duels and+0.155in teams. Harvest and delivery improvements remain uncertain. More observed meal consumption is not by itself proof of greater renewable yield, less worker starvation or a stronger colony. Swarm8 has a similar positive meal point estimate but a wide interval crossing zero, and harvested wheat falls4.779/10k[−9.550,−0.414].','', 'The fresh8/12 starvation-rate change is only−0.029deaths/10k(~2%), interval[−0.176,+0.093]; worker starvation per million worker-ticks is essentially flat. The earlier pilot’s stronger starvation improvement does not replicate clearly here. Swarm8 reduces the all-unit starvation-rate point estimate about10.8%, but its broad subject interval also crosses zero. Birth suppression and lower resource demand remain part of interpreting any starvation reduction.','', '## Alliance accounting','', 'Team outcomes are scored once per alliance. In whole-alliance2v2 telemetry,8/12 has no clear meal, starvation, worker-starvation or inn-labor improvement. Under8/8, alliance starvation falls0.394deaths/10k[−0.758,−0.116], alongside1.157fewer worker births[−2.101,−0.255] and no clear increase in meals. This is a useful secondary pressure-reduction signal, but not independent proof of a meal-allocation fix or competitive improvement. Ownership transfers between allies cancel in net alliance conversions; subject population alone is insufficient.','', '## Limits and interpretation','', '3,166of3,432games (~92.2%) end at the95% model threshold;64reach actual engine endings and202reach tickcaps. Candidate arms change which games reach each ending, so actual endings must not be compared as if a randomly selected subset. The trajectory scorer intentionally credits declared outcomes for remaining horizon; adjusted score changes are not actual victory-rate changes.','', 'Joint three-arm exact checkpoint coverage falls from935scenarios at16,384ticks, to469at32,768,162at49,152,77at65,536 and42at81,920. The late group is survival/early-stop selected. The optional full-horizon432game stage was skipped at its fixed08UTC start deadline, so no new no-prediction-stop cohort exists. Broad strength coverage is much stronger than the pilot; controlled late food-exhaustion exposure is still weak.','', 'All-case histories quantify supply activity, food consumption/harvest/delivery, production and mortality. They do not establish local renewable wheat yield for each inn, which buildings share a catchment, or the recruitment/routing decisions that initiate escalation. Broad per-building request/binding/admission histories are not available outside the six predeclared diagnostic scenarios. Score ties do not establish cap inactivity.','', 'The practical result:8/12 is a gentler operational limit than8/8, preserves birth production and has a small feeding signal, but neither is a demonstrated general strength improvement or fix for the original escalation loop. Inn8 is not isolated here. A follow-up should compare inn default/8 crossed with swarm default/8/12 across a declared broad panel, and separately guarantee sustained late observation with consistent stopping rules. Local renewable yield versus demand, staffing requests versus enrollment, and worker-admission/routing reasons would directly test the proposed mechanism. No new runs are launched by this review and policy defaults remain unchanged.','', '## Evidence','', '- [Frozen primary results](../overnight/SUMMARY.md) and [machine-readable scores/coverage](../overnight/summary.json).','- [All-case three-arm telemetry](../food-common-window/SUMMARY.md), [estimates/CIs](../food-common-window/balanced-estimates.csv), [case deltas](../food-common-window/joint-common-case-deltas.csv), and [checkpoint coverage](../food-common-window/fixed-checkpoint-coverage-and-means.csv).','- Source/bundle/framework and worker-release evidence:../../freeze-validation.json,../../root-launch-validation.json,../../completion-verification.json; helper provenance and validation in../../scripts/food-analysis.*.json.','- All parse/observation error lists are empty. Native Linux only; this review does not establish cross-platform simulation checksum equivalence.']
(out/'FULL-ANALYSIS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print(out/'FULL-ANALYSIS.md')
